;; The trap↔class table — doc/design/0022 B.5's numbered artifact. A wasm
;; trap has no exception class, so an entry where the oracle threw and a
;; compiled lane trapped compares equal only where a row says so; any
;; other pairing is a bug or a new numbered divergence.
;;
;; :jvm-message narrows the class (0023, review): ArithmeticException
;; also means long overflow ("long overflow"), which must never equate to
;; a division trap. All strings are observed, not recalled: the JVM's is
;; what `(quot 1 0)` actually throws, the engine strings verified
;; 2026-07-30 on the pinned toolchain (wasmtime 47.0.1, V8/node).
;; Row 2 matches on class alone (:jvm-message "") — StackOverflowError's
;; message is null, a recorded weakening of the jvm-message guard (0024).
[{:row 1
  :class "java.lang.ArithmeticException"
  :jvm-message "/ by zero"
  :wasmtime "integer divide by zero"
  :v8 "divide by zero"}
 {:row 2
  :class "java.lang.StackOverflowError"
  :jvm-message ""
  :wasmtime "call stack exhausted"
  :v8 "Maximum call stack size exceeded"}]
